WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:02.941
Everything here can react to sound.

2
00:00:02.941 --> 00:00:08.641
On the I O tab, the Audio section listens to a microphone, an audio file, or another tab.

3
00:00:09.095 --> 00:00:10.262
Choose Microphone.

4
00:00:10.262 --> 00:00:12.988
A test tone stands in for a real mic here.

5
00:00:12.988 --> 00:00:18.243
Linear spacing spreads the bands evenly, and the spectrum shows each beep arrive.

6
00:00:18.698 --> 00:00:20.210
Turn on the beat detector.

7
00:00:20.210 --> 00:00:24.224
Its light flashes on every hit, and Beat becomes a modulation source.

8
00:00:24.675 --> 00:00:29.220
Spectrum to Z displacement lifts each scan line by its own frequency band.

9
00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:30.387
Turn up the amount.

10
00:00:30.839 --> 00:00:32.368
Or patch sound anywhere.

11
00:00:32.368 --> 00:00:36.255
In Graph mode, the Library has an audio-reactive bloom patch.

12
00:00:36.255 --> 00:00:39.058
Load it, and the glow pumps with every beep.

13
00:00:39.521 --> 00:00:44.211
Classic slots can use Audio, a single band, or Beat as their source, too.

14
00:00:44.665 --> 00:00:49.534
Plug in a real mic, or load a song file, and the whole picture plays along.

15
00:00:49.534 --> 00:00:51.027
Next: the oscilloscope.
